wskit plans, applies, verifies and reverts the setup of Ubuntu and macOS workstations for AI coding agents. Changes are previewed unless --apply is given.

Usage:
  wskit [flags]
  wskit [command]

Commands:
  adopt            Adopt existing machine state into a unit
  disarm           Disarm an armed dead-man timer
  doctor           Check the machine's health
  explain          Explain a unit or a configuration field
  next             Show the next action for the conductor
  plan             Show the resolved setup plan
  resume           Resume an interrupted run
  revert           Revert to a restore point or to the baseline
  setup            Run setup by stage (previews unless --apply is given)
  status           Show the recorded status of every unit
  unmanage         Stop managing a unit and keep its files

Configuration commands:
  config           Show, change and check layered configuration
  interview        Answer questions to write a configuration
  migrate          Migrate configuration to the current schema

Unit commands (wskit UNIT VERB):
  accounts         The accounts unit (identity)
  agent-settings   The agent-settings unit (agent)
  agentctl         The agentctl unit (system)
  audit-agent      The audit-agent unit (ops)
  baseline         The baseline unit (system)
  browser-tunnel   The browser-tunnel unit (remote)
  firewall         The firewall unit (network)
  git-identity     The git-identity unit (identity)
  indexing         The indexing unit (system)
  machine-identity The machine-identity unit (identity)
  mcp              The mcp unit (agent)
  mesh-vpn         The mesh-vpn unit (network)
  packages         The packages unit (system)
  packages-user    The packages-user unit (system)
  remote-desktop   The remote-desktop unit (remote)
  resource-limits  The resource-limits unit (ops)
  runtimes         The runtimes unit (agent)
  shell            The shell unit (agent)
  snapshots        The snapshots unit (data)
  ssh              The ssh unit (remote)
  tools            The tools unit (agent)
  vpn              The vpn unit (network)
  workloads        The workloads unit (system)
  workspace        The workspace unit (workspace)

Additional Commands:
  completion       Print a shell completion script
  help             Help about any command
  version          Print the wskit version

Flags:
      --apply           make the changes; without it, commands only preview
      --config string   read configuration from this file
  -h, --help            help for wskit
      --json            write the result as versioned JSON on standard output and events as JSON lines on standard error
      --plain           write plain lines with no styling and no prompts (also WSKIT_PLAIN=1)
      --quiet           show only results and errors
      --stage stage     select one setup stage by its ID
      --verbose         show more detail

Use "wskit [command] --help" for more information about a command.
